1
00:00:00,699 --> 00:00:03,012
(Q11（单选）) So, hello everyone.

2
00:00:03,012 --> 00:00:11,997
My name's Lou Miller and I'm going to be your tour guide today as we take this fantastic boat trip around the Tasmanian coast.

3
00:00:11,997 --> 00:00:16,986
Before we set off, I just want to tell you a few things about our journey.

4
00:00:16,986 --> 00:00:20,242
Our boats aren't huge as you can see.

5
00:00:20,242 --> 00:00:31,515
We already have three staff members on board and on top of that, we can transport a further fifteen people – that's you – around the coastline.

6
00:00:31,515 --> 00:00:42,665
[Q11答案句] But please note if there are more than nine people on either side of the boat, we'll move some of you over, otherwise all eighteen of us will end up in the sea!

7
00:00:42,665 --> 00:00:46,011
(Q12) We've recently upgraded all our boats.

8
00:00:46,011 --> 00:00:58,485
[Q12答案句] They used to be jet black, but our new ones now have these comfortable dark red seats and a light-green exterior in order to stand out from others and help promote our company.

9
00:00:58,485 --> 00:01:03,270
This gives our boats a rather unique appearance, don't you think?

10
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:08,713
(Q13) We offer you a free lunchbox during the trip and we have three types.

11
00:01:08,713 --> 00:01:13,329
Lunchbox 1 contains ham and tomato sandwiches.&nbsp;

12
00:01:13,329 --> 00:01:17,026
[Q13答案句] Lunchbox 2 contains a cheddar cheese roll&nbsp;

13
00:01:17,026 --> 00:01:23,415
and Lunchbox 3 is salad-based and also contains eggs and tuna.&nbsp;

14
00:01:23,415 --> 00:01:29,418
All three lunchboxes also have a packet of crisps and chocolate bar inside.

15
00:01:29,418 --> 00:01:33,846
Please let staff know which lunchbox you prefer.

16
00:01:33,846 --> 00:01:39,197
(Q14) I'm sure I don't have to ask you not to throw anything into the sea.

17
00:01:39,197 --> 00:01:51,653
[Q14答案句] We don't have any bins to put litter in, but Jess, myself or Ray, our other guide, will collect it from you after lunch and put it all in a large plastic sack.

18
00:01:51,653 --> 00:02:00,561
(Q15&16（多选）) The engine on the boat makes quite a lot of noise so before we head off, let me tell you a few things about what you're going to see.

19
00:02:00,561 --> 00:02:09,039
This area is famous for its ancient lighthouse, which you'll see from the boat as we turn past the first little island.

20
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:17,387
It was built in 1838 to protect sailors as a number of shipwrecks had led to significant loss of life.

21
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:25,389
The construction itself was complicated as some of the original drawings kept by the local council show.

22
00:02:25,389 --> 00:02:30,421
It sits right on top of the cliffs in a very isolated spot.

23
00:02:30,421 --> 00:02:43,563
In the nineteenth century there were many jobs there, such as polishing the brass lamps, chopping firewood and cleaning windows, that kept lighthouse keepers busy.&nbsp;

24
00:02:43,563 --> 00:02:54,540
These workers were mainly prison convicts until the middle of that century when ordinary families willing to live in such circumstances took over.

25
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:58,907
(Q17&18) Some of you have asked me what creatures we can expect to see.

26
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:15,867
I know everyone loves the penguins, but they're very shy and, unfortunately, tend to hide from passing boats, but you might see birds in the distance, such as sea eagles, flying around the cliff edges where they nest.

27
00:03:15,867 --> 00:03:24,594
When we get to the rocky area inhabited by fur seals, we'll stop and watch them swimming around the coast.

28
00:03:24,594 --> 00:03:31,094
They're inquisitive creatures so don't be surprised if one pops up right in front of you.

29
00:03:31,094 --> 00:03:39,088
Their predators, orca whales, hunt along the coastline too, but spotting one of these is rare.

30
00:03:39,088 --> 00:03:47,531
Dolphins, on the other hand, can sometimes approach on their own or in groups as they ride the waves beside us.

31
00:03:47,531 --> 00:03:51,163
(Q19&20) Lastly, I want to mention the caves.

32
00:03:51,163 --> 00:04:00,228
Tasmania is famous for its caves and the ones we'll pass by are so amazing that people are lost for words when they see them.

33
00:04:00,228 --> 00:04:15,328
They can only be approached by sea, but if you feel that you want to see more than we're able to show you, then you can take a kayak into the area on another day and one of our staff will give you more information on that.

34
00:04:15,328 --> 00:04:17,827
What we'll do is to go through a narrow channel, past some incredible rock formations and from there we'll be able to see the openings to the caves, and at that point we'll talk to you about what lies beyond.

